68/B68-p29-winning-team.jpg","c":"OUR WINNING TEAM. H. W. Shields. D. Patience. J. Ginty. C. T. Carter. A. E. Taylor. H. E. Footer.","id":"B68-20","w":"February-March 1935"},{"f":"crops/B158/B158-p11-surrey-intercounty-team-1937.jpg","c":"27th January 1937---Part of Belgrave's winning team which beat U.S.M. (Paris) pose with Surrey's winning inter-county team at the Television studios, Alexandra Palace. But for our match in Paris coinciding with the inter-county championship, Carter,Penny,Footer and Cohen would have been included in the Surrey team. Belgravians are (l to r) rear row: W.L. Bayliss (President), A.R. Shaw. Centre row: C.T. Carter, A.W. Penny, J.A. Kemp, L.J. Cohen. Front row: A.E. Taylor, H.E. Footer. The central figure is, of course, J.C. Crump and the man on the extreme right, Denis Brickwood--then of Mitcham AC. Six days after these teams were televised by the Baird process, it was announced by the B.B.C. that the E.M.I. process would be adopted!","id":"B158-24","w":"March 1966"},{"f":"crops/B166/B166-p05-flashback-waddilove-team-1938.jpg","c":"This is part of the team that won the famous 'Waddilove' trophy at Birchfield in 1938, beating L.A.C., Blackheath, Birchfield, Polytechnic and Achilles.","id":"B166-07","w":"June 1968"},{"f":"crops/B172/B172-p06-doubleday-harley-snowballs.jpg","c":"Gordon Doubleday (left) and Alf Harley (right) try their hand at putting snow balls during one of their climbing holidays in the \"Thirties\". Alf Taylor is in the centre.","id":"B172-10","w":"December 1969"},{"f":"crops/B172/B172-p34-team-photo-with-trophies.jpg","c":"FLASHBACK TO 1934, shows Belgrave's cross-country runners and officials with their trophy collection which includes the London-Brighton (News of the World) Trophy, Southern and Surrey County cups. The team was also placed in the National and South of Thames Senior and Junior races.\nBACK ROW (l.to r.):E.A.Duffett,R.Savage,A.T.Jordan,B.Lindsey,S.T.Ring,F.R.Webb,N.Dewberry, A. Robertshaw, W. Mitchell, A. Patience, L. Rollins.\nCENTRE ROW (l. to r.):T.Eaton(masseur),D.Patience,R.Patience,J.Belchamber(Past President), W.H.Hare(Hon.Tresurer),J.R.McKay(President),W.Bayliss(General Hon.Secretary),E.Gordon(Past President),F.Walker,C.Penny,WG.Webb.\nFRONT ROW (l. to r.):W.Rice,C.T.Carter,H.W.Shields,J.Flower,A.W.Penny,S.Warboys,A.Shaw, A.Taylor,[illegible].E.Footer(Captain), A.Allum.","id":"B172-66","w":"December 1969"},{"f":"crops/B184/B184-p16-inter-counties-1934.jpg","c":"Names to fit the faces left to right are: -. Mitchell, H.W.Shields (Mx), J.E.Flower (Mx), A.Allum (Mx), W.Bayliss, A.W.Penny (Sy), A.E.Taylor (Sy), H.E.Footer (Sy), C.T.Carter (Sy).","id":"B184-41","w":"March 1974"},{"f":"crops/B202/B202-p31-1930s-national-team.jpg","c":"L to R   A.Allum, H.E.Footer, A.E.Taylor, A.R.Shaw, S.Warboys Arthur Penny, J.E.Flower, H.W.Shields, Tom Carter and W.A.Rice","id":"B202-94","w":"April 1981"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B172/B172-p06-doubleday-harley-snowballs.jpg","caption":"Gordon Doubleday (left) and Alf Harley (right) try their hand at putting snow balls during one of their climbing holidays in the \"Thirties\". Alf Taylor is in the centre.","source":"B172-10","when":"December 1969"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Alf Taylor in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1931–1993: 208 mentions in 85 issues, 126 race results and 7 photographs. Wrote or reported 1 item.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B68/B68-p29-winning-team.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-alf-taylor.html"},"legend":false}